=== SURVEY ===
Mapped web App.tsx route groups + standalone routes → 23 AppRoute cases across 7 sidebar groups, plus the
web path aliases (/battery, /battery/health, /charging/curves, /statistics, /location, /alerts, /signals,
/devtools, /account, /). Reused TSEmptyState + TSCommandPalette from the component library.

=== REASONING ===
- One AppRoute enum drives the sidebar, the iPhone tabs, deep-link parsing, the command palette, and commands.
  Each route carries pathSegment (kebab), title key, SF Symbol, and group. Parser + registry are pure + tested.
- Adaptive shell: NavigationSplitView (searchable sidebar grouped by AppRouteGroup + detail) on macOS/iPad
  regular width; TabView (4 primary tabs + a grouped "More" stack) on compact iPhone (horizontalSizeClass-gated).
- Pages (P7) plug in via AppRouteHostRegistry (environment). Until a page registers, RouteHost renders a real
  TSEmptyState ("route.pagePending") — the shell is routing infrastructure, not a fake per-page screen.
- macOS/iPad commands: ⌘1–4 quick-nav + a Navigate menu mirroring the sidebar groups, bound to the selection.
- Command palette (⌘K) lists every route; route changes post an AccessibilityNotification.Announcement.
- @Entry HARDENING: SwiftFormat auto-migrated my EnvironmentKey boilerplate to the @Entry macro, which (like
  #Preview) needs Xcode's macro plugin and fails plain swiftc. Disabled SwiftFormat's environmentEntry rule and
  kept manual EnvironmentKey (compiles on every toolchain). Same fix applied to UnitFormatters' tsUnits key.

=== CHANGES === (apps/apple/Sources/App/** unless noted)
  + AppRoute.swift           AppRoute (23) + AppRouteGroup + path/title/icon/group metadata + primaryTabs
  + AppRouteParser.swift     deep-link + alias parsing (pure)
  + RouteHostRegistry.swift  AppRouteHostRegistry + routeHosts environment (manual EnvironmentKey)
  + AppShell.swift           adaptive NavigationSplitView / TabView shell + RouteHost + command palette + recents + announcer
  + AppCommands.swift        macOS/iPad menu-bar quick-nav + Navigate menu
  ~ Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift   root now AppShell(selection:) + .commands { AppCommands }
  ~ Sources/Components/DataDisplay/UnitFormatters.swift   tsUnits reverted @Entry → manual EnvironmentKey
  ~ .swiftformat             --disable environmentEntry (keep manual EnvironmentKey; avoid macro-plugin dependency)
  + Tests/Unit/App/RouteTests.swift  unique segments, canonical/alias/URL parsing, group membership, registry round-trip

=== PARITY ===
App-shell prompt (no single page manifest). Coverage = every web App.tsx route group + alias has an AppRoute /
parser entry, and a NavigationSplitView (macOS/iPad) + TabView (iPhone) shell hosts them. No PARITY_COVERED/REQUIRED emitted.

